    "analyzer_invocation": "analyze_esc045_torch_column.py's own analyze()/compare_arm_vs_truth/format_table functions, UNMODIFIED, imported by a thin per-leg driver (not analyze.py's own CLI main()) and called once per completed leg with configs=[<that one leg's tuple>], immediately followed by deleting that leg's raw JSON dumps (keeping the shared LoRA safetensors) -- required because the pod's disk (60GB, ~26GB free after prep) was under the dispatch's 30GB threshold, and five legs' raw dumps run ~3.7GB each (~19GB total) if kept simultaneously. The five per-leg reports were concatenated (configs list extended, reordered to the analyzer's own CONFIGS order) into this artifact's 'combined_report' below -- the per-leg cosines themselves are each individually the analyzer's own unmodified output, never hand-edited."
